{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2633879","formula":"CH₆N₂O₃","hill":"CH6N2O3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"H":6.0,"N":2.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Carbamide peroxide","ru":"Гидроперит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Hydrogen peroxide–urea (also called Hyperol, artizone, urea hydrogen peroxide, and UHP) is a white crystalline solid chemical compound composed of equimolar amounts of hydrogen peroxide and urea. It contains solid and water-free hydrogen peroxide, which offers a higher stability and better controllability than liquid hydrogen peroxide when used as an oxidizing agent. Often called carbamide peroxide in dentistry and when used in over-the-counter ear drops, it is used as a source of hydrogen peroxide when dissolved in water for bleaching, disinfection and oxidation.","ru":"Гидроперит (лат. Hydroperitum) — клатрат пероксида водорода с карбамидом (мочевиной) C O ( N H 2 ) 2 ⋅ H 2 O 2 {\\displaystyle {\\rm {CO(NH_{2})_{2}\\cdot {}H_{2}O_{2}}}} . При растворении в воде получается раствор пероксида водорода и карбамида N H 2 C O N H 2 {\\displaystyle {\\rm {NH_{2}CONH_{2}}}} ."},"fame":17,"pubchemCid":31294,"mass":94.07,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(=O)(N)N.OO","inchikey":"AQLJVWUFPCUVLO-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"hydrogen peroxide;urea","classes":[{"qid":"Q107434516","names":{"en":"complex"}},{"qid":"Q5139913","names":{"en":"cocrystal","ru":"сокристалл"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-696658","atoms":52,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[4.839,0.0,0.0],[0.0,12.922,0.0],[0.0,0.0,6.761]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":3.943,"y":3.252,"z":2.418,"el":"H"},{"x":3.315,"y":3.209,"z":5.798,"el":"H"},{"x":1.524,"y":3.209,"z":4.344,"el":"H"},{"x":0.896,"y":3.252,"z":0.963,"el":"H"},{"x":0.896,"y":9.67,"z":4.344,"el":"H"},{"x":1.524,"y":9.713,"z":0.963,"el":"H"},{"x":3.315,"y":9.713,"z":2.418,"el":"H"},{"x":3.943,"y":9.67,"z":5.798,"el":"H"},{"x":3.305,"y":1.723,"z":3.034,"el":"H"},{"x":3.953,